preferred-citation:
  type: software
  title: "TCS formalizations: sunflowers, the metric TSP integrality gap, IP = PSPACE, and Toda's theorem"
  authors:
    - family-names: Lee
      given-names: Troy
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6912-2338"
  version: toda-v0.1.0
  date-released: 2026-10-15
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23382977
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of Toda's theorem, PH ⊆ P^#P, from Complexitylib's
  unchanged polynomial hierarchy and accepting-leaf-count #P definitions to a
  deterministic polynomial-time oracle machine receiving full binary answers,
  with a corollary charging every returned answer bit. The proof follows
  Fortnow's isolation and integer-amplification route through a bounded-error
  parity operator, with machine-level witness characterizations, uniform
  #P/GapP closure, affine hashing, and a costed three-query reduction.
  Developed with AI assistance; original attribution is preserved for all
  vendored sources. This component is included in the TCS formalizations
  repository.
keywords:
  - computational complexity
  - counting complexity
  - polynomial hierarchy
  - Toda's theorem
  - formal verification
  - Lean
